  "question": {
    "text": "If $P$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix such that $P^{T}=2 P+I$, where $P^{T}$ is the transpose of $P$ and $I$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix, then there exists a column matrix $\\quad X=\\left[\\begin{array}{l}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array}\\right] \\neq\\left[\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right]$ such that",
    "image": null
  },
